WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.719 --> 00:00:06.890
After a failed 2007 film adaptation, Philip
Pullman's inventive His Dark Materials series

00:00:06.890 --> 00:00:09.550
is finally set to arrive on HBO in 2019.

00:00:09.550 --> 00:00:14.480
If you're ready to see Lyra's journey translated
to the small screen, here are all the details

00:00:14.480 --> 00:00:17.000
you need to know before His Dark Materials
premieres.

00:00:18.100 --> 00:00:22.960
Philip Pullman's first His Dark Materials
book, published as The Golden Compass in America,

00:00:22.960 --> 00:00:26.900
tells the story of Lyra, a young girl who
lives in a world with "daemons," which are

00:00:26.900 --> 00:00:29.869
counterparts of a person's soul that take
the form of an animal.

00:00:29.869 --> 00:00:34.660
Lyra and her daemon Pantalaimon [pant-uh-LIE-mon]
discover evidence of "Dust," mysterious particles

00:00:34.660 --> 00:00:39.000
that are more attracted to children than adults,
leading them on a grand adventure.

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:42.740
Lyra also gains possession of the titular
golden compass, which is technically called

00:00:42.740 --> 00:00:46.610
an alethiometer, which can discern the truth
in any situation.

00:00:46.610 --> 00:00:50.930
The two continue their journey, eventually
meeting Will, a boy from a different dimension.

00:00:50.930 --> 00:00:54.640
As the three journey on in the subsequent
novels, The Subtle Knife and The Amber Spyglass,

00:00:54.640 --> 00:00:59.329
they find more universes, make new friends
and enemies, and even "kill God."

00:00:59.329 --> 00:01:03.260
That last plot point, unsurprisingly, has
stirred up some controversy since the first

00:01:03.260 --> 00:01:04.790
novel was published in 1995.

00:01:04.790 --> 00:01:10.110
Pullman, an avowed atheist, has staunchly
defended his series throughout the years,

00:01:10.110 --> 00:01:14.390
sticking to his guns about his allegories
and subject matter without hesitation.

00:01:14.390 --> 00:01:18.120
Thanks to the popularity of the books, an
adaptation didn't take very long.

00:01:18.120 --> 00:01:21.060
In 2007, The Golden Compass arrived in theaters.

00:01:21.060 --> 00:01:25.850
One of New Line Cinema's most expensive productions
to date, it underperformed at the North American

00:01:25.850 --> 00:01:27.620
box office upon its release.

00:01:27.620 --> 00:01:32.210
Despite a talented cast and Academy Award-winning
special effects, the movie failed with audiences

00:01:32.210 --> 00:01:33.260
and critics alike.

00:01:33.320 --> 00:01:36.920
With plenty of creative unhappiness behind
the scenes and loud dissent from the Catholic

00:01:36.920 --> 00:01:38.980
Church, the movie did not get a sequel.

00:01:39.880 --> 00:01:43.700
The original Golden Compass film might have
faltered when it came to the plot, but its

00:01:43.700 --> 00:01:48.180
casting choices were pretty excellent, leaving
a new cast with big shoes to fill.

00:01:48.180 --> 00:01:51.580
Luckily, the new adaptation has recruited
a stacked cast of its own.

00:01:51.580 --> 00:01:56.510
James McAvoy will step into Lord Asriel's
calculating and intimidating shoes, and will

00:01:56.510 --> 00:02:01.100
spend some time on screen with Luther's Ruth
Wilson, who will be playing the secretly insidious

00:02:01.100 --> 00:02:02.100
Mrs. Coulter.

00:02:02.100 --> 00:02:06.820
Hamilton creator Lin-Manuel Miranda, who was
last seen on-screen in Mary Poppins Returns,

00:02:06.820 --> 00:02:11.009
will take over the role of Lee Scoresby],
the affable aeronaut [AIR-oh-not] who helps

00:02:11.009 --> 00:02:12.370
Lyra throughout her journey.

00:02:12.370 --> 00:02:16.700
The cast will be rounded out with familiar
faces like Clarke Peters, Ariyon Bakare, and

00:02:16.700 --> 00:02:17.700
many more

00:02:18.080 --> 00:02:22.640
If you thought there was plenty of starpower
in front of the camera for His Dark Materials,

00:02:22.640 --> 00:02:24.880
wait until you hear who's working behind the
scenes.

00:02:24.880 --> 00:02:28.709
The series will be written by Jack Thorne,
who cut his teeth on shows like Skins and

00:02:28.709 --> 00:02:32.310
Shameless, as well as films like Wonder and
A Long Way Down.

00:02:32.310 --> 00:02:35.400
From there, he moved to the stage and, alongside
writer J.K.

00:02:35.400 --> 00:02:39.290
Rowling and co-writer John Tiffany, Thorne
wrote the script for the play Harry Potter

00:02:39.290 --> 00:02:40.450
and the Cursed Child.

00:02:40.450 --> 00:02:44.380
The first two episodes of the series will
have an even bigger Hollywood darling at the

00:02:44.380 --> 00:02:45.380
helm.

00:02:45.380 --> 00:02:49.349
Academy Award-winning director Tom Hooper,
who won an Oscar for The King's Speech and

00:02:49.349 --> 00:02:53.530
followed that up with Les Miserables, will
kick off the series just before his adaptation

00:02:53.530 --> 00:02:57.099
of Cats hits the big screen during the 2019
holiday season.

00:02:57.099 --> 00:03:00.930
In short, fans of the books can rest assured
that His Dark Materials will have plenty of

00:03:00.960 --> 00:03:01.480
talent working behind the scenes.

00:03:03.600 --> 00:03:07.980
Of course, one of the most important roles
in the series is that of Lyra, the plucky,

00:03:07.980 --> 00:03:11.890
brilliant, and brave heroine who inspired
millions of fans as they made their way through

00:03:11.890 --> 00:03:13.160
the original books.

00:03:13.160 --> 00:03:17.660
On the heels of Dakota Blue Richards, who
made her film debut with the role in the 2007

00:03:17.660 --> 00:03:21.680
film adaptation, it was clear that producers
would need to find a young actress who feels

00:03:21.680 --> 00:03:23.270
wise beyond her years.

00:03:23.270 --> 00:03:28.120
In March of 2018, it was announced that Dafne
Keen would step into Lyra's formidable shoes.

00:03:28.120 --> 00:03:32.069
If that name sounds at all familiar to you,
it's probably because you saw her breakout

00:03:32.069 --> 00:03:36.470
role in Logan alongside Hugh Jackman in his
final appearance as Wolverine.

00:03:36.470 --> 00:03:40.980
Keen made her mark playing Laura, Logan's
clone daughter in an emotional and grounding

00:03:40.980 --> 00:03:46.100
performance that made her an obvious choice
to pick up Lyra's alethiometer for the series.

00:03:46.320 --> 00:03:51.180
Naturally, His Dark Materials made its way
to the holy grail of pop culture conventions,

00:03:51.180 --> 00:03:52.970
San Diego Comic-Con, in July.

00:03:53.520 --> 00:03:57.120
There, a few more details were announced about
the upcoming series to keep fans on their

00:03:57.120 --> 00:03:57.560
toes.

00:03:58.220 --> 00:04:01.900
Miranda, known for his musical roles, announced
that he'll bring some song and dance to the

00:04:01.909 --> 00:04:05.690
show by entering the series with a performance
co-anchored by his daemon.

00:04:05.690 --> 00:04:09.430
Wilson, for her part, revealed that the show
delves into Mrs. Coulter's backstory which

00:04:09.520 --> 00:04:11.160
should provide new insight for fans.

00:04:12.240 --> 00:04:18.240
"Philip Pullman gave us a nice in to dig a
bit deeper into her and see who she is on

00:04:18.240 --> 00:04:19.700
her own, with her monkey, without Lyra."

00:04:21.650 --> 00:04:24.480
The minds behind the project also assured
audiences that the show wouldn't explicitly

00:04:24.480 --> 00:04:30.180
criticize religious institutions, choosing
instead to attack broader authoritarian concepts.

00:04:31.280 --> 00:04:35.270
One of the chief complaints about the 2007
adaptation of The Golden Compass was that

00:04:35.270 --> 00:04:39.800
the movie tried to keep everything far too
light, with studio executives actively pushing

00:04:39.800 --> 00:04:43.400
for a "happy ending" and looking for an upbeat
finale for the first film.

00:04:43.400 --> 00:04:48.419
Luckily, according to Pullman, the BBC and
HBO have no such qualms about happy endings.

00:04:48.419 --> 00:04:52.710
Pullman has granted his permission for the
books, which rely heavily on Victorian elements,

00:04:52.710 --> 00:04:57.690
to be twisted and modernized for the adaptation,
reinventing the story for today's audiences.

00:04:57.690 --> 00:05:01.930
For fans who grew up with the books and disliked
the most recent adaptation, they may be able

00:05:01.930 --> 00:05:05.840
to rest easy and enjoy a more sophisticated
take on these beloved novels.

00:05:05.840 --> 00:05:10.270
We'll have to see what that looks like when
the series arrives some time in Fall 2019.

